<Base title="About Bukjum | Recycled materials marketplace" description="Learn about Bukjum's marketplace approach and founding recycled plastic supplier."><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT BUKJUM</p><h1>A clearer way to<br /><em>source circular materials.</em></h1><p>Bukjum connects recycled material suppliers with buyers through practical information and direct quotation requests.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container about-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">OUR APPROACH</p><h2>Useful details.<br /><em>Honest expectations.</em></h2></div><div class="about-copy"><p>We are building a marketplace for recycled materials, starting with a founding supplier offering PP, HDPE and PET flakes. Our focus is to make product condition, minimum quantities and indicative pricing visible before a buyer starts a conversation.</p><p>The founding supplier has combined production capacity of at least 50 tonnes per month across all three materials. PP is approximately 90% of output, with continuous production. Exact PET and HDPE split and product sizes are not yet confirmed.</p><p>The supplier collects, sorts and crushes plastics. Material is not washed before crushing; flakes are sold in bags and buyers should carry out additional cleaning. Delivery is available within Nigeria. Current buyers include Chinese firms in Lagos and Ogun States.</p><div class="notice-box"><strong>Illustrative image</strong><p>Images on this website illustrate recycling and sorting generally. They do not represent the founding supplier's actual factory or workers.</p></div></div></div></section></Base>
